  "reserved_endpoint_note": "ADR-0043 `<socket>.revoke` outcomes Without a `configured` field the peer's UID, principal, actor, target and ticket are exactly those of the frame; with it, the producer is configured with that actor/target/ticket instead (forged-binding cases). dispatch: the revoke reaches the output gate. Any other expect value is the reply error code, and nonce_echoed says whether that reply carries the request nonce (it does only for an authenticated well-formed frame). No method other than revoke_output_lease is ever dispatched. Over-size and deadline cases are generated by the producer tests, not stored.",
